  <running_head>INSTITUTIONUM</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>actio fed paffio cordis, qua quiescens ab</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>il-labente sanguine diftenditur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">§. 1. De pulsu cum multa Medici &amp;</l>
    <l n="4">Philosophi quoque speciatim differant</l>
    <l n="5">speciale hoc theorema formavimus:</l>
    <l n="6">quod ut explicetur, primum infpicie-</l>
    <l n="7">mus <i>quid pulsus sit,</i> &amp; <i>quas partes habeat,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">tum <i>a qua causa</i> dependeat, porro <i>quem</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>finem</i> habeat, ac denique <i>quomodo</i> fiat.</l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Pulsus cordis</i> itaque <i>est motus cordis in</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>animali ipsi secundum naturam conve-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>niens.</i> Atque de hoc nemo dubitat:</l>
    <l n="13">pulsum autem eum motum dixerunt,</l>
    <l n="14">tum quia pectus pulsat, tum quia san-</l>
    <l n="15">guinem propellit in universum corpus.</l>
    <l n="16">Ejus partes duas constituerunt, <i>systolen</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">seu <i>contractionem</i>, &amp; <i>diastolen</i> seu <i>dila-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>tationem</i>, verum autopsia monstrat in</l>
    <l n="19">differentiis vivorum, quod sola sy-</l>
    <l n="20">stole seu contractio cordis motus fit,</l>
    <l n="21">verum diastole incipiat cum actionis</l>
    <l n="22">iftius remissione, &amp; perficiatur a san-</l>
    <l n="23">guine in cordis sinus effuso.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">§. 2. Circa causam efficientem pul-</l>
    <l n="25">sus id quaeritur: <i>An ab aliqua insita</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>virtute, an ab aliquo forinsecus incidente</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>oriatur?</i> Arbitror omnino a virtute</l>
    <l n="28">quadam insita fieri. Nam si in diffe-</l>
    <l n="29">ctione vivorum praecifo mucrone cor-</l>
    <l n="30">dis digitus in ventriculos ejus immittatur</l>
    <l n="31" type="foot" para="true">tatur</l>
  </main_text>
